 /*
- * SWEET SE7 FIFO I2C / GT9896 Yellowstone / Focaltech 54:52 bring-up.
- * Call once after the scheduler is running; all work runs on one thread.
- * Requires ABL-loaded GENI I2C firmware; votes L11C through sweet_rpmh.c.
- * No firmware/config upload or direct PMIC writes. Only IC data write:
- * zero to GT9896's event status after reading a report. See touch2/report.md.
+ * SWEET (polaris) touch: Synaptics S3330 on QUPv3 SE14.
+ *
+ * The Mi Mix 2S touch controller (S3330, JDI incell panel) is on GENI I2C
+ * SE14 (DT qupv3_se14_i2c, i2c@a98000, 7-bit address 0x20), with reset on
+ * TLMM GPIO 99, IRQ on GPIO 125 and the I/O rail (tp_vddio_vreg) enabled by
+ * GPIO 23 (SOUTH pin bank). The GENI I2C firmware is the one XBL leaves
+ * loaded (protocol 3, 32-bit FIFOs), exactly what the vendor kernel expects;
+ * this driver does no firmware/config upload and no panel-rail writes.
+ *
+ * The controller speaks Synaptics RMI4.  A register access is:
+ *   write 0xFF, page      (page-select register)
+ *   write <low address>, then repeated START + read (read)
+ *   write <low address>, <data>                    (write)
+ * The PDT is scanned for F01 (identification) and F12 (2D touch); F12
+ * reporting is enabled with ctrl28 = 0xff and the data registers are polled
+ * (10 ms) into the SweetHIDTouch service.  The IRQ line is only configured,
+ * not used, so a missed edge can never wedge input.
+ *
+ * Coordinates are scaled from the F12 sensor maximum to the 1080x2160 panel
+ * (SweetHID.cpp presents that same native size under sweetfb_native=1).
  */
